% THEME A, ff tutti, bars 305-320 (= 105-120), then the close 321-324 (= 133-134, 137-138), leading on V into the coda.
% c023: close cut from 8 to 4 bars: the dying motive x no longer stops on E pp with an empty bar and then restarts at the same pitch
%   in the same cellos at the coda; the cellos' V (328) leads straight into the coda's i (329) (A&S PDF 585: rhythm, texture and dynamics shape a join).
% c022: 315 viola B+A, Hn 1 B, Hn 2 F sharp (as sC 111).

% c024: Fl 1 takes the upper octave in 309-312 and 317-320 (Rimsky-Korsakov PDF 118: a recurring tutti is rescored by extending its range; Ex. 205-206), so the reprise tutti is not a copy of 105-120
% c052: 305 Fl 1 G5 on beat 1 (was E5 with the theme): the soprano seventh A5 of the V7 at 304 resolves by step in its own register; Vln I leaps to the theme's E5
%   (A-S PDF 406-407 sec. 9, Ex. 24-11: a transferred resolution needs the tone of resolution in the same register).
